# regression_bug — FCM cm-firebase-token 401 race on logout (pre-existing, unrelated to NEARS-3518)

emulator-5558, debug build, logged in as customer@nears.com -> tapped Logout -> Yes.

I/flutter ( 4190): [NET] POST endpoint=/api/v1/auth/logout
I/flutter ( 4190): [INFO] msg="FCM registration id obtained"
I/flutter ( 4190): [NET] POST endpoint=/api/v1/auth/guest/request
I/flutter ( 4190): [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/auth/logout http_status=200
I/flutter ( 4190): [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/cm-firebase-token http_status=401
I/flutter ( 4190): ----------------FIREBASE CRASHLYTICS----------------
I/flutter ( 4190): The following exception was thrown unhandled api response:
I/flutter ( 4190): ApiFailure(status: 401)
I/flutter ( 4190): #0      ApiClient.handleResponse (package:nears/api/api_client.dart:1309:22)
I/flutter ( 4190): #1      ApiClient._send (package:nears/api/api_client.dart:866:14)
I/flutter ( 4190): [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/cm-firebase-token http_status=401 type=ApiFailure msg="unhandled api response" correlation_id=558e6708-f2fc-456d-b850-43bd0b02a6be
I/flutter ( 4190): [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/auth/guest/request http_status=200

Analysis: an in-flight FCM-token-registration call fired with the OLD (now-invalidated)
bearer token, landing AFTER the server already invalidated the session on logout ->
401. Properly logged via AppLogger.failure (paired, non-silent), not a silent-failure-path
violation. `cm-firebase-token` / the logout token-invalidation order are outside NEARS-3518's
blast radius (api_client.dart / pusher_helper.dart / app_constants.dart / android manifest /
ios entitlements / chat_controller.dart / auth_controller.dart's clearConversationState hook /
payment webviews) — pre-existing race, not introduced by this change. Non-blocking; flagged
for the PO as a regression candidate, not filed against this ticket.
